d6f39ea617a27aed53ec","ma-c-e4e3063e82c3f42f703c","ma-c-e5c9c2eb0804cd06866a","ma-c-e86c7dd71980ddbff6f9","ma-c-f61e60910e694de5bc1c","ma-c-f90d96e8de9cde2ae6df","ma-c-fa31f35fbb673f5b8941","ma-c-fee595d873594ca9c3dd"],"leaves":["ma-c-056dedd59ce376d86d51","ma-c-0e6311d63041ed4d873d","ma-c-1a8fd1c5753aaac10b97","ma-c-1c35dfe9f6e0f28fcb9a","ma-c-2f92b7909abab9853a59","ma-c-3066703587a9ac54e4e2","ma-c-3891270a8cc40de7782c","ma-c-3b31ce85d4d300199fd9","ma-c-45ae12dbc5519c1de7b3","ma-c-741728009a4f2950cfa5","ma-c-79952d3d0bc378c115ac","ma-c-7a3b7eecd0724af65fb7","ma-c-7d4bdea6dfadbd820a9b","ma-c-7e4b3c7a82dcd1b4fb58","ma-c-8d21ed1fd5564ab384c6","ma-c-92650daa92e475689648","ma-c-980a46f37ca9af432b28","ma-c-9c829b0d2aa2e3c35a1c","ma-c-9e4d3c386d1b1e826db6","ma-c-a2bba8f98618a41a267d","ma-c-aa72d84d27f0f79d29bd","ma-c-b046182a53012810e85f","ma-c-cc4ea2ff138247b4f376","ma-c-d35d658a54e248afb614","ma-c-d6f39ea617a27aed53ec","ma-c-e4e3063e82c3f42f703c","ma-c-e5c9c2eb0804cd06866a","ma-c-e86c7dd71980ddbff6f9","ma-c-f61e60910e694de5bc1c","ma-c-f90d96e8de9cde2ae6df","ma-c-fa31f35fbb673f5b8941","ma-c-fee595d873594ca9c3dd"],"papers":{"arXiv:2504.07482":{"abstract":"In one of our previous articles, we outlined the formulation of a version of the categorical arithmetic local Langlands conjecture. The aims of this article are threefold. First, we provide a detailed account of one component of this conjecture: the local Langlands category. Second, we aim to prove this conjecture in the tame case for quasi-split unramified reductive groups. Finally, we will explo","authors":["Xinwen Zhu"],"year":"2025"},"arXiv:1703.07288":{"abstract":"These notes are devoted to a detailed exposition of the proof of the Geometric Satake Equivalence for general coefficients, following Mirkovic-Vilonen.","authors":["Pierre Baumann","Simon Riche"],"year":"2017"},"arXiv:1005.4512":{"abstract":"We describe (braided-)commutative algebras with non-degenerate multiplicative form in certain braided monoidal categories, corresponding to abelian metric Lie algebras (so-called Drinfeld categories). We also describe local modules over these algebras and classify commutative algebras with finite number of simple local modules.","authors":["Alexei Davydov","Vyacheslav Futorny"],"year":"2010"},"arXiv:1108.6267":{"abstract":"Using techniques from the homotopy theory of derived categories and noncommutative algebraic geometry, we establish a general theory of derived microlocalization for quantum symplectic resolutions. In particular, our results yield a new proof of derived Beilinson-Bernstein localization and a derived version of the more recent microlocalization theorems of Gordon-Stafford and Kashiwara-Rouquier as ","authors":["Kevin McGerty","Thomas Nevins"],"year":"2011"},"arXiv:1806.07519":{"abstract":"Truncated shifted Yangians are a family of algebras which naturally quantize slices in the affine Grassmannian. These algebras depend on a choice of two weights $λ$ and $μ$ for a Lie algebra $\\mathfrak{g}$, which we will assume is simply-laced. In this paper, we relate the category $\\mathcal{O}$ over truncated shifted Yangians to categorified tensor products: for a generic integral choice of param","authors":["Joel Kamnitzer","Peter Tingley","Ben Webster"],"year":"2018"},"arXiv:1603.05593":{"abstract":"We introduce various affine Grassmannians, study their geometric properties, and give some applications. We also discuss the geometric Satake equivalence. These are the expanded lecture notes for a mini-course in 2015 PCMI summer school. References updated and more details added.","authors":["Xinwen Zhu"],"year":"2016"},"arXiv:2505.17953":{"abstract":"We compute the dimension of the cohomology of stalks of intersection cohomology complexes on Zastava schemes and Drinfeld compactifications associated with a connected reductive algebraic group $G$, in case the characteristic of the coefficients field $\\Bbbk$ is good for $G$. In particular, we show that these dimensions do not depend on the choice of $\\Bbbk$.","authors":["Pramod N. Achar","Gurbir Dhillon","Simon Riche"],"year":"2025"},"arXiv:0711.0793":{"abstract":"We show that if A is an abelian category satisfying certain mild conditions, then one can introduce the concept of a moduli space of (semi)stable objects which has the structure of a projective algebraic variety. This idea is applied to several important abelian categories in representation theory, like highest weight categories.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Marcos Jardim","Adriano Moura"],"year":"2007"},"arXiv:0801.0903":{"abstract":"We address two problems regarding the structure and representation theory of finite W-algebras associated with the general linear Lie algebras. Finite W-algebras can be defined either via the Whittaker model of Kostant or, equivalently, by the quantum Hamiltonian reduction. Our first main result is a proof of the Gelfand-Kirillov conjecture for the skew fields of fractions of the finite W-algebras","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Alexander Molev","Serge Ovsienko"],"year":"2008"},"arXiv:2609.21644":{"abstract":"We develop a categorical framework for Lie-Rinehart monoids and their weak modules in a symmetric monoidal category. Using crossed homomorphisms, we construct a natural action of the monoidal category of modules over a Lie monoid on the category of weak Lie-Rinehart modules, thereby obtaining categorical versions of the Shen-Larsson functors. We further characterize the conditions under which the ","authors":["Han Dai","Vyacheslav Futorny","Huimin Gao"],"year":"2026"}}}